==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ang|fled}}, {{l|ang|flett}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*flatją||floor}}, from {{der|ang|gem-pro|*flataz||flat}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*plat-||flat}}. Akin to {{cog|ofs|flet|flet, flette|dwelling, house}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|ang|/flet/}}

====Noun====
{{ang-noun|n|flet}}

# the [[floor]], [[ground]]
#: ''Heó on '''flet''' gecrong'' &mdash; She sank to the ground.
# a [[dwelling]], [[habitation]], [[house]], [[cottage]], [[hall]]
#: ''Gif ðæt '''flet''' geblódgad wyrþe.'' &mdash; If the house be stained with blood.

=====Declension=====
{{ang-decl-noun-a-n|flet}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ang|fletræst}} f. — couch
* {{l|ang|fletsittend}} m. — sitter in hall, courtier, guest.
* {{l|ang|fletwerod}} n. — hall-troop, body-guard

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|enm|flet}}
** {{desc|en|flet}}

===Etymology 2===
Likely from {{der|ang|gem-pro|*flutōną||to float}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*plewd-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*plew-||to float, swim, fly}}; compare {{cog|da|fløde||cream}}, {{cog|is|fleytið||skimming}}, {{cog|no|fløte||cream}}

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|ang|flete}}, {{l|ang|fliet}}, {{l|ang|flyte}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|ang|/fleːt/}}

====Noun====
{{ang-noun|head=flēt|f|flēta}}

# [[cream]], [[skimming]], [[curds]]
#: ''Hwít sealt dó on reám oððe góde '''fléte'''. &mdash; Put white salt into cream or good skimmings.

